<section class="section section--alt">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head">
      <span class="section__eyebrow">Why Westside Baptist Academy</span>
      <h2>A small school that knows your child by name.</h2>
      <p class="section__lede">Westside Baptist Academy opened in {{ site.founded }} as a ministry of {{ site.church.name }}. What has not changed since is the reason we exist: to come alongside Christian parents rather than replace them.</p>
    </div>

    <ul class="marks">
      <li><strong>Christ-centered instruction</strong><span>Scripture is not a subject added to the schedule. It is the framework every subject is taught inside of.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Low student-to-teacher ratios</strong><span>Teachers know each student's strengths, gaps and character &mdash; and so do their parents.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Rigorous academics</strong><span>A college-preparatory curriculum that graduates students ready for what comes next.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Strong standardized testing</strong><span>Annual achievement testing keeps our academics honest and measurable.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Consistent character training</strong><span>Expectations are clear, applied evenly, and reinforced by the same adults every day.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Chapel each week</strong><span>Corporate worship and preaching are a normal part of the school week.</span></li>
      <li><strong>A full fine arts program</strong><span>Choir, orchestra, ensembles and art &mdash; taught, not treated as an afterthought.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Qualified, ministry-minded faculty</strong><span>Our teachers are here because they believe in the work, not because it was the job available.</span></li>
    </ul>

    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn" href="/about/">More about the Academy</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

